#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* `surface`. This is the CSS-only\nform of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand button, a\nprimary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a fixed inverse token,\nit picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the surface changes."
msgstr "Y blaen darllenadwy — du neu wyn — ar gyfer cynnwys a osodir *ar* `surface`. Dyma ffurf sy'n gweithio gydag CSS yn unig o amrywiadau adlewyrchol `*-on-color` InstUI (cylch ffocws ar fotwm brand, testun botwm cwbl-ffrâm, eicon ar wyneb lliw): yn hytrach na thocyn gwrthfelin sefydlog, mae'n dewis y gwrthgyferbyniad o'r wyneb ei hun, felly mae'n aros yn gywir wrth i'r wyneb newid."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and snaps it to `0` (black) or\n`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no JS, no fixed hex."
msgstr "Mae'n darllen goleuedd OKLCH y wyneb drwy sintacs lliw perthynol ac yn ei gynnig i `0` (du) neu `1` (wyn) yn `threshold` gan ddefnyddio triciwn clamp `calc(… * infinity)` — dim JS, dim hex sefydlog."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The background colour content sits on (literal, `var(--token)`, or a nested helper)."
msgstr "Y lliw cefndir y mae cynnwys yn gorwedd arno (llythrennol, `var(--token)`, neu gynorthwyydd mewnol)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "OKLCH lightness (0–1) above which the surface counts as \"light\" (default `0.62`)."
msgstr "Goleuedd OKLCH (0–1) uwch na hynny y mae'r wyneb yn cael ei ystyried yn “golau” (diofyn `0.62`)."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An `oklch(from …)` expression resolving to black or white."
msgstr "Mynegiad `oklch(from …)` sy'n dadfoddi i du neu wyn."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Flatten `overlay` (at `percent`% strength) over an opaque `base` — a CSS-only stand-in for\nui-color-utils `overlayColors`. That helper source-over-composites two RGBA colors into one opaque\nresult; the common case (a translucent tint over a solid surface) is exactly a two-color\n`color-mix()`. General RGBA-over-RGBA compositing can't be a single CSS color, so this covers the\nopaque-base case only."
msgstr "Llafnwch `overlay` (yn `percent`% cryfder) dros `base` aneglur — sef ateb CSS-yn-unig ar gyfer\nui-color-utils `overlayColors`. Mae’r cynorthwyydd hwnnw’n cyfuno dwy liw RGBA mewn un ganlyniad bregus; y sefyllfa gyffredin (ton gwyn ysgafn dros arwyneb solet) yw union\n`color-mix()` o ddau liw. Ni all cyfuniad cyffredinol RGBA-dros-RGBA fod yn un lliw CSS sengl, felly mae hyn yn cwmpasu’r achos sylfaenol aneglur yn unig."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The opaque background color."
msgstr "Y lliw cefndir aneglur."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/overlayColors.md
